## Do

- Put business logic in `src/service/{{kebabCase name}}.service.ts`; keep the router thin.
- Define new shapes in the contract slice; derive variants with `.pick()/.omit()/.extend()`.
- New Drizzle tables in `src/schema/index.ts` (always with `tenantId`), then `pnpm regen`.
- Add routes with `pnpm gen route {{kebabCase name}} <METHOD> <path>`; admin handlers call
  `await adminGuard.assert(context)` first (the plugin passes `c.get(ADMIN_GUARD)` to the factory).
- Cross-module reads: import another add-on's tables via `@blurifycom-addons/<name>/schema`
  (read-only). For synchronous money/answers use a command port (eg `WALLET_COMMANDS`).
- Emit events AFTER the DB commit via the injected `EventBus`; use `emitInTransaction` for
  durable money-critical events.

## Don't

- Import another add-on's root or internals (lint errors). Talk via events / command ports /
  contracts / the `/schema` subpath.
- Call a vendor SDK / `fetch` directly - define a port + adapter.
- Throw HTTP errors from the service - throw domain errors, map them in the router.
- Import another `@blurifycom-addons/*` package (cross-add-on imports are lint errors).
- Define ad-hoc Zod in `router/` or use `any` (both lint-enforced).
